{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Concern map of `_store/event_append.py` re-measured on origin/main @1c3e945cb8 (794 LOC, 6 under the 800 cap — premise HOLDS; tonight's `staging.py` extraction already landed at 267 LOC and is composed with, not duplicated).\n\nFour concerns remain, each a clean call-graph seam:\n\nA. PRE-LOCK EVENT PREPARATION (~111 LOC) — `EVENT_TYPES`, `StoreError`, `event_filename`, `_ensure_initialized`, `_validate_event`, `_prepare_event`. Pure: no lock, no git, no subprocess. Sole downstream edge is `staging.stage_event` + `canonical.canonical_bytes`. Leaf.\n\nB. BOUNDED / RETRY-COMPOSED GIT VERBS (~189 LOC) — `_GIT_TIMEOUT`, `_run_git`, `_TRANSIENT_ADD_MARKERS`, `_GIT_ADD_ATTEMPTS`, `_GIT_ADD_BACKOFF_S`, `_is_transient_add_error`, `_with_transient_add_retry`, `_git_add`, `_git_commit`, `_git_rm`, `_git_commit_paths`, `_restore_paths`, `_unstage`. Every lock-held git child funnels through `_run_git`; the verbs compose gitutil's index.lock + HEAD-parse retries with the local object-DB retry. Depends only on `gitutil` (shared) + `subprocess`. Leaf.\n\nC. COMMIT-FAILURE SELF-HEAL (~127 LOC) — `_REGENERABLE_PREFIX`, `_recover_from_unmerged`, `_INVALID_OBJECT_MARKERS`, `_is_invalid_object_error`, `_staged_index_paths`, `_recover_from_invalid_object`.\n\nD. LOCKED WRITE ORCHESTRATION (~200 LOC) — `delete_events`, `stage_and_commit`, `batch_stage_and_commit`, `write_and_push`, `batch_write_and_push`, `_rollback_batch`, `_maybe_enrich_drain`, `_silent_unlink`. Owns all three `lock.write_lock(..., retries=...)` sites and the push/enrich hand-off.\n\nCUT: extract A and B; keep C with D.\n\nWhy C stays with D (deliberate seam choice, not incompleteness): `_recover_from_invalid_object` and `_recover_from_unmerged` both re-issue `_git_add` on their retry path, and `tests/interfaces/store/test_event_append_transient_retry.py` (`test_own_vanished_object_is_regenerated`) does a SINGLE `monkeypatch.setattr(event_append, \"_git_add\", ...)` that today is observed by both `stage_and_commit`'s add and the recovery re-add through one module global. Splitting C out would put those two callers in different namespaces and silently decouple the seam. C is also intrinsic to the commit step it heals, so `event_append` = \"the locked write transaction and its commit-failure self-heal\" is a coherent concern, not a residue.\n\nWhy B is separate from the existing `gitutil.py`: `gitutil` is the retry machinery SHARED with `_commands/txn.py`; B is the write path's own bounded verb set that composes it. `gitutil.py` is also being edited concurrently by unheedful-custodial-bluebottle — B is a new leaf that IMPORTS gitutil and does not touch it.\n\nProjected: `event_append.py` 794 -> ~500 (~300 LOC headroom under cap); `event_prepare.py` ~140; `event_commit_git.py` ~220. No module under 100.\n\nBinding-preservation set enumerated (grep for both dotted and string-literal forms over tests/ + src/): every external consumer reaches these through the `event_append` namespace — `EVENT_TYPES`, `StoreError`, `event_filename`, `delete_events`, `stage_and_commit`, `batch_stage_and_commit`, `write_and_push`, `batch_write_and_push`, `_run_git`, `_git_add`, `_GIT_TIMEOUT`, `_is_transient_add_error`, `_INDEX_LOCK_STALE_S`, `_maybe_enrich_drain`, `_lock`, `subprocess`. All re-exported; zero test edits.\n\nStructural gates checked against the cut: `.github/complexity-baseline.json` has no `event_append` keys (no path-key churn); `check_raw_git_writes.py` sanctions by INLINE `# raw-git-ok:` marker with no external allowlist (markers move with the code); `test_lock_retry_zebrafish::_opt_in_sites` asserts `{\"event_append.py\": 3, ...}` — all three `write_lock(retries=)` sites are in concern D and stay put."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786604891758953001,"uuid":"1b7cd6fb-3b2a-4874-ae0e-ea2ed8285606"}